   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: 1. The government rehabilitates and upgrades the road network on South
Tarawa. 
Indicator: By April 2013, 27.5 km of paved road and 6 km of unpaved road rehabilitated or upgraded to maintainable condition (average road roughness index no higher than 3 by 2013)
Rehabilitated or upgraded roads are:
(i)	St. Anne to airport (21.5 km) and Temaiku spur (2.8 km)
(ii)	Betio and Bikenibeu roads (repairs)
(iii)	Betio Causeway (3.2 km)
(iv)	Feeder roads (6 km) 
Progress/Status: (i) Revised St. Anne(Bairiki) - airport (21.5km) and Temaiku spur (6.1km) - Achieved 35.5kms of paved road improved (increased over the original target due to increase in Betio)
(ii) Betio and Bikenibeua roads (repairs) - achieved 11.4 km unpaved road paved.
(iii) Betio loop and main road - achieved 1.8kms unpaved road improved
(iv) Betio causeway -removed in 2015 from scope. 
Data Source: MFED&amp;apos;s quarterly progress reports 
Target year: 2013</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: 2. Community-based enterprises have the capacity to maintain the road network. 
Indicator: By May 2013, 6 community-based enterprises contracted to undertake road maintenance covering 45 km of road network 
Progress/Status: Maintenance approach changed to subcontracting 3 subcontractors engaged to cover whole road due to difficulties in establishing and recruiting enterprises in each community. Subcontractors are performing satisfactorily, including following road safety guidelines and practices. 
Data Source: MFED&amp;apos;s quarterly progress reports 
Target year: 2013</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: 3. The MPWU provides efficient implementation support. 
Indicator: Physical works completed by April 2013 within budget 
Progress/Status: Physical works completed on 28 November 2016 within revised budget following additional financing and project changes in 2015 and 2016. 
Data Source: MFED&amp;apos;s quarterly progress reports 
Target year: 2013</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Outcome</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The population has sustainable access to a safe, well-maintained road network in South Tarawa.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adequate financing for road maintenance (base $1,000 per km, target $1,500 per kilometer by 2013) 
Progress/Status: --An annual budget of A$0.5 million is currently being provided up to November 2018 when the defects notification periods ends. A draft concept note for a Cabinet paper has been prepared addressing road maintenance options for 2019 and beyond, citing the need for A$0.415 million for annual maintenance. 
Data Source: Government accounts</narrative>
    </description>
